# Why Learn APIs?

Modern software applications rarely work in isolation.

Whenever you:

- Log into an application
- Book a flight
- Order food online
- Make a payment
- Watch a movie
- Use Google Maps
- Check your bank balance
- Send a WhatsApp message

multiple APIs work together behind the scenes.

Understanding APIs enables testers and developers to verify these interactions accurately and efficiently.

---

# Why API Testing Matters

API Testing is one of the most valuable testing skills in the software industry.

Unlike UI testing, API Testing validates the application's business logic directly, making it faster, more reliable, and less affected by user interface changes.

Organizations increasingly rely on API Testing because it helps identify defects early, improves software quality, and supports continuous integration and continuous delivery (CI/CD) pipelines.

